{"id": "en_story_apollo13", "tag": "SPACE", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#FFC83D", "lang": "en", "total": 70.83, "segments": [{"text": "3 brave astronauts face a sudden terrifying survival emergency far away from home in deep space.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.36}, {"text": "It is April 1970 and Apollo 13 flies high on its vital flight to the Moon.", "start": 5.96, "end": 10.08}, {"text": "About 56 hours into the flight an oxygen tank in the service module suddenly explodes.", "start": 10.66, "end": 15.0}, {"text": "Jack Swigert radioes Okay Houston we've had a problem here back to the ground team.", "start": 15.82, "end": 19.3}, {"text": "Jim Lovell repeats the message as the entire dangerous situation turns critical for all 3 men.", "start": 19.92, "end": 24.06}, {"text": "The planned Moon landing is cancelled immediately as staying alive becomes their only main mission goal.", "start": 24.6, "end": 28.84}, {"text": "Jim Lovell Jack Swigert and Fred Haise move directly into the lunar module named Aquarius.", "start": 29.56, "end": 34.06}, {"text": "They use the small lunar module Aquarius as a temporary lifeboat in deep cold space.", "start": 34.56, "end": 38.82}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide rises dangerously inside because the required air filters do not fit together at all.", "start": 39.76, "end": 44.22}, {"text": "The command module's square filters do not fit into the lunar module's round sockets at all.", "start": 44.88, "end": 48.88}, {"text": "Engineers on the ground quickly design a fix with plastic bags cardboard and duct tape.", "start": 49.6, "end": 53.76}, {"text": "This makeshift fix works perfectly and keeps all 3 brave astronauts breathing safely in space.", "start": 53.76, "end": 58.3}, {"text": "The entire brave crew finally splashes down safely back on Earth on 17 April 1970.", "start": 58.96, "end": 63.64}, {"text": "Could you remain completely calm if your life depended on 